{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/916730-devotion-query-force-of-nature","id":916730,"title":"Devotion Query: Force of Nature","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-18T01:46:46-07:00","id":916730,"title":"Devotion Query: Force of Nature","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The description of Force of Nature states, <br /> <br /> &quot;When activating Force of Nature, the vampire gains as</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">many of the advantages of Predatory Aspect, Beast\u2019s Skin,</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">and Unnatural Aspect as she wishes, without Vitae costs. She</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">can adopt additional modifications or shed existing ones as a</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">reflexive action. As well, with an instant action, she can shift</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">a number of Physical Attribute dots equal to her Protean to</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">other Physical Attributes. These change derived traits, and can</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">exceed her normal limitations.&quot;<br /> <br /> I was wondering whether the exceed normal limitations would mean that a blood potency 10 elder could then, by shifting attributes, temporarily have strength above 10 before even taking vigor into account?</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11998-gascoigne","name":"Gascoigne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T13:22:56-07:00","id":916962,"title":"","content":"Story-teller's discretion. I'd say the limitations leveled at a character as the result of her Blood-Potency would be her &quot;normal limitations.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11970-panopticon","name":"Panopticon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T14:02:36-07:00","id":916977,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the reply, I agree with your take on &quot;normal limitations&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11998-gascoigne","name":"Gascoigne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T16:48:24-07:00","id":917039,"title":"","content":"I'd say the opposite. This is how the power is described :<br /> <br /> &quot;When the vampire activates Force of Nature, her body becomes a mess of rapid change. She grows and loses limbs in the blink of an eye. Her skin becomes rock solid, then gelatinous within moments. She\u2019s truly protean; she changes the way water flows. However, she needs the strength of Resilience to protect her form from collapsing in upon itself.&quot;<br /> <br /> To me, when that power is in effect, the vampire is no longer constrained by what a humanoid shape is capable of. So yeah, I'd say you could totally exceed your normal limitations. You'd just look like some total freak with oversized arms on a skeletal frame (if you transfered from stamina to strength for example. Besides, the amount of dots you can tranfer is &quot;only&quot; your score in protean (which is 5), so while it's a great boost, it's not absurd either. It only gives you the passive benefit of Vigor 5 for a scene, and your other physical stats suffer while you keep that up. Sure, it's a really powerful devotion, but it's expensive, requires a bunch of high level disciplines that are not all in the same clan and costs 8 vitae to activate.<br /> <br /> My last point would be that it's only really likely to be an issue if your character has huge strength to begin with. If we're talking about a blood potency 10 vampire, they can just as well spend 15 vitae to boost their strength by 30 for a single turn. Sure, it's shorter, but if we're talking about a single opponent, a measly 5 strength boost doesn't really change much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T18:23:52-07:00","id":917076,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;These change derived traits, and can </span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">exceed her normal limitations.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> There are no limitations besides the users Protean dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T07:30:19-07:00","id":918026,"title":"","content":"A quick question about this Devotion... can a vampire shift her Vigor- and Resilience-gained dots as well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Don't follow me, I'm lost too! But if you do...</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","name":"Gimmisky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11263_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T07:51:23-07:00","id":918036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gimmisky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/916730-devotion-query-force-of-nature?p=918026#post918026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A quick question about this Devotion... can a vampire shift her Vigor- and Resilience-gained dots as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T16:38:27-07:00","id":918303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gimmisky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/916730-devotion-query-force-of-nature?p=918026#post918026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A quick question about this Devotion... can a vampire shift her Vigor- and Resilience-gained dots as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>Options.<br /> <br /> * Yes.<br /> Rational: Because the stat boost from both of these disciplines are passive, the Kindred would &quot;feel&quot; that these traits are natural. This suggests that shifting these values with a Devotion that requires them to function in the first place would be as natural as shifting any other accessible values within the Devotion's preview.<br /> <br /> *No.<br /> Rational: The Devotion does not clearly state that it has the power to shift values acquired via other Devotions or Disciplines and is thus not within it's sphere of influence.<br /> <br /> *Sure?<br /> Rational: Since it's still limited by the Kindred's understanding of Protean, it's not really a game changer but does allow the player to Role-play through an awesome moment in a fashion her character was clearly designed to handle... <br /> <br /> (Edit)<br /> <br /> *Maybe.<br /> Rational: A few things need to come together first. Does it fit the Theme? Will it clash terribly with the Mood? Is it your ST who is doing it with an NPC (if so, bring lube)? Is it one of your players do it with their character? Do you use a table voting system on elements of a game-line that are not clearly defined? etc. You can just play it by ear with your group. <br /> <br /> Alternative: If we're going to allow it to effect values acquired by these two Disciplines, then it can ONLY effect the values acquired by these two Disciplines. <br /> <br /> * Ta hell with da mechanics!: Alright, the character is now a flying spaghetti monster that can preform Heracles feats of strength. Lets just role-play all of the psychological elements afterwards here. How do these actions make the character feel? Was it frenzy? Was she riding the wave? What do the witnesses think and how does it make them feel? What about your &quot;friendly&quot; neighborhood Masquerade? Did the character just join the freak show that is the front page of the Supermarket tabloids? How will this act of badassory impact her Requiem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11970,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11970-panopticon","user":"Panopticon","date":". 06-21-2016, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11970-panopticon","name":"Panopticon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T23:39:53-07:00","id":918464,"title":"","content":"According to me simply not cause Vigor is supernatural strenght, not linked to muscle or mass. Protean allows you to modify your shape (your muscles and mass) to enhance your strenght.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T04:14:27-07:00","id":918545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gimmisky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/916730-devotion-query-force-of-nature?p=918026#post918026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A quick question about this Devotion... can a vampire shift her Vigor- and Resilience-gained dots as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pg. 141 &quot;Add the vampire\u2019s dots in Vigor to her Strength&quot;<br /> The wording is a bit ambiguous but it appears that the Strength gain from Vigor (likewise Resilience-Stamina) is a derived bonus, not an actual Attribute dot gain. I would rule no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T05:45:39-07:00","id":918573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/916730-devotion-query-force-of-nature?p=918464#post918464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to me simply not cause Vigor is supernatural strenght, not linked to muscle or mass. Protean allows you to modify your shape (your muscles and mass) to enhance your strenght.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does a vampire gain muscle mass when she buys a normal dot of Strength?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}